# Mobile app — per-machine settings. Copy to .env and fill in as needed.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Every value here is OPTIONAL. A fresh clone runs with none of them set.
# This file is committed; .env is not.

# Where the Next.js API is reachable from your PHONE.
#
# Leave unset and it auto-detects this computer's LAN address, which is right
# in almost every case. Set it when auto-detection picks the wrong interface
# (VPN, Docker, several adapters), or when the API is not on your machine.
#
# Never "localhost" — on a physical device that means the PHONE's own
# localhost. Your phone and computer must be on the same Wi-Fi.
#
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://192.168.1.42:3000

# Only the port, if the web server is not on 3000 (host is still detected).
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_API_PORT=3000

# --- Only needed to BUILD the app with EAS -----------------------------------
# Not needed to RUN it against a dev client you already have installed.
#
# Get these by running `npx eas-cli init` in this directory: it creates a
# project under your own Expo account and writes the id here for you.
#
# Do not copy someone else's id. You cannot build against a project you do not
# own — EAS refuses it with "Entity not authorized", which reads like a broken
# login rather than the permissions problem it actually is.
#
#   EAS_PROJECT_ID=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
#   EXPO_OWNER=your-expo-username
